      "math_academy_id": "q-47084",
      "sequence_position": 8,
      "problem": "Consider the function $f(x)=(x-1)(x+1)(x-2).$ For which of the following values of $k$ does the intermediate value theorem **not** guarantee that $f(x)=k$ has a solution on the interval $[0,3]?$",
      "worked_solution": "The function $f(x)$ is continuous on $[0,3],$ therefore, the intermediate value theorem guarantees that $f(x)=k$ has a solution for each value of $k$ between $f(0)$ and $f(3).$\n\nSince $f(0)=2$ and $f(3)=8,$ we must have \n$k\\in [2,8].$\n\nAmong the given options, only $k=0$ does not belong to the interval $[2,8].$",
